---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = '/apps/attentive';
const title = 'Attentive review for Shopify stores';
const desc = 'Evaluate acquisition and coordinated messaging across the channels your account and recipients can actually use. Fit depends on permission, workflow readiness and a current quote, rather than revenue cutoffs.';
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Does Attentive only offer SMS?",
    "answer": "No. Its current supplier page lists email, SMS, MMS, RCS and push options. Verify selected channels and account entitlements."
  },
  {
    "question": "Is there a minimum store revenue?",
    "answer": "No universal revenue cutoff is established here. Evaluate required capabilities, a current quote and operating capacity."
  },
  {
    "question": "Is every subscriber reachable on RCS or push?",
    "answer": "No. Check recipient country, carrier, device support, setup and channel permission separately."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does two-tap signup prove consent for every channel?",
    "answer": "No. Inspect the actual collection flow and purpose-specific permission record for each channel."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can I keep another email platform?",
    "answer": "Evaluate explicit ownership and timely suppression across systems. Rehearse cancellation and retries before running live journeys."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does supplier support guarantee compliance or a launch date?",
    "answer": "No. Confirm service scope, review relevant markets and set launch criteria from readiness checks. No fixed implementation duration is established."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <a class="link" href="/apps">← All app reviews</a>
    <p class="editorial-kicker mt-6">Supplier scope checked November 25, 2026</p>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Attentive review for Shopify stores</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9">Evaluate acquisition and coordinated messaging across the channels your account and recipients can actually use. Fit depends on permission, workflow readiness and a current quote, rather than revenue cutoffs.</p>
    <p class="mt-5">The workflows below are proposed acceptance checks, not merchant engagements or measured vendor outcomes.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black">Current channels, packages and positive capabilities</h2>
      <p>Attentive’s <a href="https://www.attentive.com/pricing">current pricing page</a> offers modular messaging plans across SMS, MMS, email, RCS and push. It describes two-tap signup, cross-channel journeys, campaign tools and support. Pricing depends on message volume, subscriber count, selected channels and AI tools. These capabilities make acquisition and coordinated messaging useful evaluation areas; no store-revenue threshold establishes fit.</p>
      <p>Confirm purchased entitlements, merchant location, recipient country, carrier and device support before treating a channel as available. A package listing does not mean every recipient can receive RCS or push. Separate product availability from a subscriber’s current channel permission. Supplier claims about uplift are not results for the merchant being evaluated here.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black">Proposed beauty acquisition and device matrix</h2>
      <p>For a hypothetical beauty brand using paid-social landing pages and influencer drops, rehearse mobile signup before replacing capture tools. Compare equivalent traffic and consent wording; record eligible visitors, completion, permission provenance and subsequent opt-outs. Two-tap signup is a current supplier capability, but a faster-looking interaction does not establish higher incremental profit.</p>
      <p>Test iOS and Android, desktop, an in-app browser, a blocked popup, a returning subscriber and an incomplete signup. Inspect the actual confirmation and permission record rather than counting a button click as a completed subscription. Verify that email capture does not silently subscribe the person to SMS, RCS or push.</p>
      <p>Include an unsupported device or country and a person who declines one channel while accepting another. Define fallback only for a separately eligible destination; do not silently move an undeliverable promotional message to another channel. Keep the existing acquisition path if the proposed replacement loses required context or has an unresolved accessibility or identity issue.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black">Pop-up retail, QR and Shopify identity</h2>
      <p>Proposed pop-up fashion scenario: a location-specific QR code opens a signup experience, and a later Shopify or POS order should link to the correct customer. First verify the configured integration and fields; a location tag is not proof of consent. Have the event owner use the reviewed collection language and record its version and source.</p>
      <p>Rehearse a shared household phone, a typo, a repeat visitor, a visitor who buys before the welcome delay and a person who opts out at the event. Check how customer matching resolves conflicting identifiers. Route ambiguous records to review instead of merging them based on a similar name. Do not assume every POS sale automatically supplies a messageable identity.</p>
      <p>Assign a separate owner for event signage, signup configuration, data sync and follow-up content. Reconcile actual signup records against the event source before enabling offers. Retail staff improvising verbal permission cannot be fixed by attributing compliance responsibility to the vendor.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black">Cart, purchase and channel collision checks</h2>
      <p>For a hypothetical fashion cart journey, write down the email and SMS owners, intended delays and purchase cancellation rule. Confirm that the chosen account supports the proposed journey and data inputs. Do not infer that a shared platform automatically prevents every duplicate. Email opens alone are an unreliable reason to send an escalation.</p>
      <p>Test email-only permission, SMS-only permission, both, neither and opt-out during delay. Then test purchase immediately before dispatch, refund after purchase, delayed order sync and duplicate cart events. Inspect sends and cancellations in each active platform. A nightly segment exchange may be too stale for a short cart delay; measure the configured latency and block activation when it cannot meet the cancellation requirement.</p>
      <p>When retaining another ESP, define which system owns welcome, recovery, post-purchase education and winback. Sharing a customer profile does not authorize both queues to send. Pause the incumbent sequence before activating the replacement, with a rollback plan that avoids reviving abandoned work.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black">AI, sale-day edits and country readiness</h2>
      <p>If the selected package includes the required optimization tools, compare a proposed optimized broadcast against a fixed-window control among eligible recipients. Balance time zones and establish local sending restrictions, exclusions and observation windows before assignment. Audience size alone does not prove statistical significance or guarantee lift.</p>
      <p>For a Black Friday preview, rehearse VIP access, a last-minute stock change, recent-purchaser exclusion and a recalled offer. Inspect the final destination, content, schedule and channel on staff records. Record operator effort and rollback behavior. Do not assume managed services can execute every urgent edit or that support guarantees delivery by a particular deadline.</p>
      <p>Confirm country-specific setup and sender readiness with the supplier for each intended market. Have appropriate reviewers assess collection and message purposes in that market. Compliance tools can support operations, but vendor involvement does not establish legal adequacy. Include an unreachable RCS recipient and check the documented behavior rather than assuming SMS fallback is enabled or permitted.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black">Quote, service scope and retain-or-replace decision</h2>
      <p>Request a written quote covering channel units, carrier charges, list size, seasonal peaks, AI products, support scope, onboarding, term, minimums if any, overages and exit/export terms. Model a quiet month and a sale month. The current supplier page describes usage-based pricing and modular packages; no $500 platform floor or $2,000 contract estimate is asserted here.</p>
      <p>Compare the configured incumbent against the same acquisition and journey requirements. Keeping Postscript for SMS and another ESP for email, consolidating, or retaining the current arrangement are conditional choices. A beauty or supplement store need not graduate at a revenue or subscriber count. Select the arrangement whose verified capabilities and total operating cost meet the merchant’s needs.</p>
      <p>Launch by readiness rather than a four-to-twelve-week promise. Confirm ownership, permission evidence, integration fixtures, sender readiness, export access and operator training. Set a review date appropriate to the campaign cycle, with explicit stop conditions for duplicate sends, missing suppression or incomplete permission records. No mandatory ninety-day pilot or fixed return multiple is implied.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black">Cutover and rollback are acceptance gates</h2>
      <p>Proposed procedure: inventory active campaigns, automations, scheduled sends and retry queues before moving any audience. Assign one owner for each event and channel. Pause old entries and cancel or drain queued messages before enabling replacements. A shadow comparison can inspect events without sending; a parallel live cart sequence risks duplicate contact.</p>
      <p>Persist stable event keys to deduplicate retries and historical replays. Check current order, refund, suppression and channel permission again at dispatch. Stop the rollout if identity cannot be reconciled or a purchase fails to cancel recovery. Keep an export of configuration and permission provenance, a named rollback owner and a way to disable the new sender without reactivating stale queues.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black">Measure contribution and operator effort</h2>
      <p>Use staff fixtures to establish behavior before measuring commercial effects. For a live evaluation, define eligible recipients, assignment, observation window and returns treatment before launch. Compare equivalent groups or a randomized holdout where feasible. Attributed revenue is a reporting view; it does not show how much would have happened without the message.</p>
      <p>Illustrative planning arithmetic, not a supplier price or observed result: four hours saved monthly at $50 per hour minus $100 additional monthly cost yields $100 net monthly benefit. A $1,200 setup cost then takes twelve months to recover. At two hours saved, net benefit is zero and that payback disappears. Replace each input with a quote, measured labor and incremental contribution; include discounts, returns and ongoing maintenance.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black">Continue the comparison</h2>
      <p>Use these related reviews and guides to define alternatives against the same requirements; the links do not establish a capability winner.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><a class="link" href="/apps">Apps</a></li>
        <li><a class="link" href="/apps/postscript">Apps · Postscript</a></li>
        <li><a class="link" href="/apps/klaviyo">Apps · Klaviyo</a></li>
        <li><a class="link" href="/for/high-aov">For · High Aov</a></li>
        <li><a class="link" href="/compare/klaviyo-vs-postscript">Compare · Klaviyo Vs Postscript</a></li>
        <li><a class="link" href="/apps/omnisend">Apps · Omnisend</a></li>
        <li><a class="link" href="/compare">Compare</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Attentive Shopify FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
